+All evidence is verified against run events, the workspace copies of `.fabro/workflows/develop/workflow.fabro` / `prompts/*.md` / `scripts/evidence.nu`, and `.fabro/run-painpoints.jsonl`. Run totals for context (from the run's conclusion event): 19m29s wall, $0.658, 936.8k tokens (736.8k cache-read), 15 stage executions, final status `failed(workflow_error)` — despite one seed (`fabro-8d26`) being implemented, gated green, and approved.
+
+## Recommendations, ordered by expected impact
+
+**1. The 12KB preamble budget is smaller than what the reviewer must read — raise it.**
+- **What happened:** `evidence.nu` emitted a 6,378-byte capture (both cycles, byte-identical blob `3794…`). The reviewer keeps tester+evidence history (`preamble_stages_ignore="planner,implementer,reviewer"`), so by cycle 2 its preamble held two ~6.4KB captures — over `preamble_budget_kb=12` before anything else. The renderer spilled both to ~400-char previews + blob paths the tool-less reviewer can't open. reviewer@1 correctly held ("verification-uncertainty"); reviewer@2 then **approved without ever seeing the diff**, judging on "convergent secondary signals" (its own painpoint). The no-op rework cycle this caused (planner@3 + implementer@3 + tester@2 + evidence@2 + reviewer@2) cost **$0.209 and ~5 min — 32% of the run**.
+- **Change:** `.fabro/workflows/develop/workflow.fabro` line 6: `preamble_budget_kb=12` → `20`–`24`. The seed `fabro-d810` itself said "adjust AFTER first measurement if 12KB cuts real evidence (evidence node outputs can legitimately be 6-7k)" — this run is that measurement. Also correct the now-false claims at workflow.fabro lines 79–84 and `prompts/reviewer.md` line 11 that `summary:high` "carries the evidence capture in full" — the budget spill overrides fidelity, as this run proved.
+- **Effect:** review verdicts grounded in the actual diff; eliminates the ~$0.21/5-min verification-hold cycle and the silent rigor loss of ungrounded approvals.
+
+**2. Add a planner→refiner "Blocked" edge — this single missing edge is why the run is red.**
+- **What happened:** planner@4 routed `preferred_next_label="Blocked"` on the fabro-d810 deadlock; the graph has no such edge (planner exits are lines 127–129; "Blocked" exists only on implementer→planner, line 132). The hold rode `outcome=failed`, tripped `goal_gate=true` on planner, and the run concluded `workflow_error: "goal gate unsatisfied for node planner and no retry target"` — despite fabro-8d26 being closed successfully minutes earlier.
+- **Change:** add `planner -> refiner [label="Blocked", condition="preferred_label=\"Blocked\""]` after line 128, and add a Blocked output variant (`outcome: "succeeded"`, label `Blocked`, `failure_reason` carried in context) to `prompts/planner.md`'s outcome contract so the goal gate stays satisfied.
+- **Effect:** deliberate human-escalation stops failing runs; the ledger distinguishes "blocked for a human" from genuine planner errors.
+
+**3. Model the cross-world blocker on seed fabro-d810 — 35% of this run re-derived a known-dead state.**
+- **What happened:** planner@1 spent ~2.5 min proving the seed infeasible (`which fabro` → not found, no run-event store under `.fabro/`, no meta world; events seq 74–91); planner@4 spent 263s/$0.148 with 12,756 reasoning tokens re-deriving the same conclusion plus "Validated: 4 well-formed entries". `sd ready` still lists fabro-d810 as priority-1, zero blockers.
+- **Change:** in the tracker (seed `fabro-d810` in `.seeds/issues.jsonl` via `sd`): add the `sd dep` on the denkhaus fabro-29f7 rebuild sequence (or drop its priority below implementable seeds / label it `blocked-external`), and paste the infeasibility facts into the seed description so the next planner reads them instead of re-proving them.
+- **Effect:** saves ~$0.26 and ~7 min of deadweight planner reasoning per run until the denkhaus rebuild lands; also prevents a naive planner from claiming it and deadlocking the implementer.
+
+**4. Add an "Evidence retry" verdict so a delivery failure doesn't re-run the whole pipeline.**
+- **What happened:** reviewer@1's feedback explicitly said "No code change is implied … re-run the evidence stage or relay the full capture (blob 3794…)", but `prompts/reviewer.md` (lines 30–60) offers only Approved / Changes requested, and `changes_requested` forces planner→implementer→tester→evidence→reviewer. The diff was byte-identical across both cycles — implementer@3 ($0.075, 105s) verified an unchanged worktree.
+- **Change:** third route in `prompts/reviewer.md` ("Evidence retry": `outcome: succeeded`, `preferred_next_label: "Evidence retry"`) plus edge `reviewer -> evidence [label="Evidence retry"]` in workflow.fabro.
+- **Effect:** a re-delivery costs 0.3s (evidence script) + one review call (~$0.03) instead of ~$0.21 and 5 minutes.
+
+**5. Stop reviewer.md from telling the reviewer it has tools.**
+- **What happened:** `prompts/reviewer.md` line 13 says "re-run `just qualitygate` yourself — you have tools", while line 1 of the same file (and the node's `shape=tab`) declares it tool-less. The reviewer's own painpoint flags exactly this contradiction.
+- **Change:** delete the "you have tools" clause; state the gate result is visible only via the tester stage section.
+- **Effect:** free correctness fix in the same file you're editing for #4; removes a hedge the model can't act on.
+
+**6. Verification-only briefs must not mandate the gate the implementer is forbidden to run.**
+- **What happened:** planner@2/@3 briefs listed `just qualitygate` under "Required verification commands"; implementer.md rule 4 forbids running the full gate. implementer@3 had to resolve the contradiction itself and filed painpoint #3 (present in `.fabro/run-painpoints.jsonl`).
+- **Change:** one sentence in `prompts/planner.md`'s verification-only guidance: "list smoke-level commands only (`go build`, `go test`, `go run` smokes); the gate belongs to the tester stage."
+- **Effect:** removes an unsatisfiable checklist item that could route a healthy seed to Blocked.
+
+**7. Treat user-abort/infra death as cancellation, not a deterministic Blocked bounce.**
+- **What happened:** implementer@2 received the German steer "beende den run" plus Docker 409 mid-verification; it returned `outcome=failed` (category `deterministic`), bounced to planner, and spawned a full extra cycle. Its failure signature sits in `loop_failure_signatures` as deterministic, and its German reply ("Verstanden — ich beende den Run…") leaked into later stages' context.
+- **Change:** (a) one line in `prompts/implementer.md`: "Always respond in English"; (b) platform-side painpoint (already implicit in the ledger): classify user-stop/container-death as cancel/transient and halt the run instead of routing Blocked→planner.
+- **Effect:** a stop request actually stops; no phantom deterministic-failure signature pollutes the next run's preamble.
+
+**8. Stop echoing the full painpoint list through every agent.**
+- **What happened:** all three prompts require "restate the full accumulated list" (last-writer-wins). By planner@4 that's 4 entries ≈ 2.8KB mirrored into three prompts per pass, part of its 263s went to "Validating: 4 well-formed entries", and the reviewer received the list itself truncated — accumulation is lossy at exactly the node told to restate it.
+- **Change:** since `refiner.nu` already delivers from the append-only `.fabro/run-painpoints.jsonl`, change the painpoint sections in all three prompts to "emit only NEW entries" and have the planner append them directly to the file; drop the restate-the-world instruction.
+- **Effect:** frees ~3KB of the 12KB preamble budget (compounds with #1), removes the lossy restatement loop, trims planner reasoning overhead.
